<http://purl.org/spar/biro> a ns1:Vocabulary ;
    dcterms:creator <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5506-523X>,
        <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-0530-4305> ;
    dcterms:description "BiRO, the Bibliographic Reference Ontology, is an ontology structured according to the FRBR model to define bibliographic records (as subclasses of frbr:Work) and bibliographic references (as subclasses of frbr:Expression), and their compilations into bibliographic collections such as library catalogues, and into bibliographic lists such as reference lists in journal articles, respectively."@en ;
